<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Azerbaijan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Azerbaijan is a region of the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> and north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, centred historically on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a>. It was the heartland from which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid dynasty</a> rose and an important base of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>. It was repeatedly contested between Iranian and Ottoman forces and later lost by Iran to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/azerbaijan.jpg" alt="Azerbaijan" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SKopp and others · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Azerbaijan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Osman fought the Anatolian ruler Kadi Burhan al-Din, whom he defeated and killed in 1398, and the rival Qara Qoyunlu, the ‘Black Sheep’ Turkmens of <b>Azerbaijan</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Azerbaijan</b>'s railway and air blockade crippled an economy that received 85 percent of its cargo by rail, Turkey closed its border in 1993, and the shutdown of the Metsamor nuclear plant in 1989 brought an energy crisis; GDP fell nearly 60 percent between 1989 and 1993, the dram,…</blockquote><a href="/empire/armenia">Armenia · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Caucasian Albania, known in Armenian as Aghvank and later in Arabic as Arran, lay in the eastern Caucasus between the Greater Caucasus range, the Caspian Sea and the Kura river, roughly in the north and centre of modern <b>Azerbaijan</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/caucasian-albania">Caucasian Albania · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>From 1262 the khans fought the Ilkhanate of Persia over <b>Azerbaijan</b> and the Caucasus, a war that drew Berke into alliance with the Mamluk sultan Baybars.</blockquote><a href="/empire/golden-horde">Golden Horde · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Hulagu made Maragha in <b>Azerbaijan</b> his capital, later supplanted by Tabriz, and adopted the title “Ilkhan”, usually understood as a subordinate khan acknowledging the supremacy of the Great Khan.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Crown Prince Abbas Mirza, governor of <b>Azerbaijan</b>, tried to create a European-style infantry, the nezam-e jadid, with help from French and British officers, but Iran lost the Russo-Persian War of 1804–1813, which ended with the Treaty of Gulistan and the loss of Georgia, Dagestan and most of the…</blockquote><a href="/empire/qajar-iran">Qajar Iran · Military</a></li></ul></section>
